    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-19T09:26:19+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-19T09:26:19+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-18T22:56:19Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-18T22:56:19Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A slow-moving high pressure system over the Tasman Sea extends a ridge over eastern SA. A trough of low pressure over western SA is moving eastwards and will reach southeastern parts later today while a weakening cold front crosses the Bight. The trough lingers in the east through the middle of the week as a weak high pressure system forms in the Bight. This trough weakens on Thursday as a second trough moves into the west from WA.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower south of Woomera, becoming less likely in the afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the late morning and afternoon. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds in the late afternoon and evening. Winds northwest to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending southeast to southwesterly in the early afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures 31 to 37.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower south of Woomera in the early morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding east of Stuart Highway in the morning and early afternoon. Winds southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 12 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 29 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers north of Coober Pedy, most likely in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Coober Pedy, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
